Z||000001||Haze_Performance||03-20-2001||12:58 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Hartz:<BR><B>So now that Mr. Mike's has discontinued a number of their products, what's everyone doing for things like carpet, headliners, etc.?  Any good leads?<P>Hartz<BR>'85 SE 3.1L V6 Turbo<BR>'84 SC 5.7L V8</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I re-did my headliner with a kit from PepBoys (Auto Parts Store)<P>I ordered my carpet last week from The Fiero Store. (+ Door carpet)<P>Im still looking for a less $$$ sunvisor. (But Mr. Mikes still sells those  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> )<P><BR><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank><BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ttttttt.gif">     </A>       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>Pennock's Fiero Forum Members Photo Page</A><BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1431213" TARGET=_blank><BR>Photopoint Gallery</A>||||reg||14
Z||000002||hugh||03-20-2001||06:52 AM||||Any auto shop that does auto interiors can do all you need.Headliners,sunvisors,etc.I had the headliner done in my GN last year.It cost $100,looks like new.How much would the material cost and how much is your time worth?Also,what about the difference there may be in the quality of the job. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroJoe||03-20-2001||07:48 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by hugh:<BR><B>Any auto shop that does auto interiors can do all you need.Headliners,sunvisors,etc.I had the headliner done in my GN last year.It cost $100,looks like new.How much would the material cost and how much is your time worth?Also,what about the difference there may be in the quality of the job. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thats what I had done this past summer.  They did a great job, took maybe an hour, and they matched the color quite well.  I didnt get my sunvisors done, so you can tell the difference in color.<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Carrolles||03-20-2001||08:21 AM||||Recovering the sunvisors is no big deal.  Use the same fabric that you use on the headliner (got all the materials including the 3M Foamfast 74 spray adhesive at a local Fabric store).  Glue it to the cardboard and sew it around the edge (fold the edge under) with a standard sewing machine, just go real slow.  They end up being a bit thicker than original but I did my headliner and sunvisors in my 85SE for around $20 and a few hours of work.<P>My wife and I will do her 85GT soon and will also recover the rear bulkhead with the same fabric because the fuzzy stuff on it now looks like cr*p.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Tina||03-20-2001||09:54 PM||||My carpet came from 1A Auto   $95 <A HREF="http://www.1aauto.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.1aauto.com</A> <P>Looks good, but not yet installed.<BR>Sunvisor<BR>Gonna have them done by a upholstery shop.<BR>Too though to sew myself.Doing it in leather.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tina.gif"> <P>Good luck<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Ironhorse||03-20-2001||10:34 PM||||Tina, those carpet that you ordered from 1A Auto actually pre molded to fit in Fieros?  2 of my brothers has ordered pre molded carpet for their 64 impala and 87 Geo Tracker. They turn out to be flat piece of carpet that you have to cut to size yourself.  I'm tryin to avoid same problem.  TIA for answer||||reg||1
Z||000007||Tina||03-20-2001||10:45 PM||||Your lucky I'am in a good mood today.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Alrighty, took the stuff out of box.<BR>Looks molded to me.<BR>Darn things won't lay flat.<BR>Only thing I noticed, that the Rubberthingy<BR>a.k.a. heel something is not black but grey.<BR>And a bit smaller. <P>BTW Got the salt and pepper color.<p>[This message has been edited by Tina (edited 03-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||Songman||03-20-2001||11:42 PM||||I had the headliner and sun visors done last year in my Aerocoupe Monte Carlo for $70. Of course, it has T-tops so the headliner is pretty small.<P>I let the guy do the 442 at the same time so he knocked off a little as a multi-car discount.<P>Check your local shops. Some of them do great work.. and they can match the fabrics perfectly. It is a lot cheaper than ordering something and doing it yourself.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
